applies here with the following readings, which take the place of the parts of it that name the files and releases of
tau-lang-demos:

1. Materials. In this repository, "Materials" means the file `AXIOM.md` and every file added to this repository later
   that does not carry its own license text. This file (`LICENSE`) states the terms. The lists of Method, Tutorial and
   Classic Materials in section 1 of the full text, and its sentence on the archive, name files of tau-lang-demos; none
   of those files is in this repository. The Materials of this repository are Tutorial Materials in the sense of section
   1 of the full text (the default class).

2. What the Materials are (section 4 of the full text). This repository contains a document. It contains no
   specification files, no part specifications, no wiring table, no queries and no records. This license makes no
   statement that any system is fair, secure, or free of operator influence.

3. All other parts of the full text apply as written, including the definitions in section 1 (among them "Commercial
   Use", "Training" and "takes the Materials"), Tau Language and other works (section 2), the Method (section 3), the
   free grants (section 5), other Commercial Use and the agreement in section 8 (sections 7 and 8), what is not claimed
   and the patent paragraph (section 9), and the general terms (section 11).

4. Attribution (section 5 of the full text): keep this file with every copy or substantial portion of the Materials; its
   reference to the full text stands for "this license text". Credit "Taumorrow" in derived works, deployments and
   republications. Suggested wording: "based on work by Taumorrow (axiom)".

5. Earlier versions (in place of section 10, items 1 and 2, of the full text).
   - Releases of this repository before commit 6cd4cc0 shipped without a license text. This text does not change what
     applies to them.
   - Commit 6cd4cc0 (3 October 2026) carried the full text of the Taumorrow Demos License v3.0; that release remains
     under v3.0.
   - Commit 31634492655869ddb4c621b5c37883b48cbdf2d2 (5 October 2026) carried the text of v3.1, with a grant for an
     ecosystem named there; that release remains under v3.1.
   - Rights granted under those texts are not revoked by this one. Nothing here is retroactive.
   - Items 3 and 4 of section 10 of the full text apply: future releases may carry different terms, and each release
     carries its license in the `LICENSE` file at that commit. If you build on the Materials, pin a commit.

